codemap 9
tour feature-dismiss-comment
kind flow
author ai
group features/gui
note The human, after reading the agent's reply under a comment, or after deciding an open question no longer needs an answer. Goal: the map is the second channel beside the source, so a settled question should leave it. Without this feature every answered box stays under its note or between its Source lines, the top bar keeps counting it, and the only way out is deleting the comment's file by hand in a directory inside .jj/repo or the git common dir that the human never sees. Dismissal is the human's act and never automatic: the reply may be wrong or incomplete, and only the person who asked knows whether it answers the question. dismiss on a green box and withdraw on an orange one delete the comment's file at once, the same way add-comment writes it, and the status line says which. Withdraw exists because a question the human answered for themselves would otherwise sit in the agent's next 'comments' list. The GUI scenario 'comments' dismisses the answered comment and checks its box is gone. Why comments exist and the designs that were tried are in feature-add-comment.

